From 7676a8fd95cc6ed2d14aa3d8d48a6f6d34e743ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cliffhall <cliff@futurescale.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 01:14:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat: security-advisory skill; rewrite SECURITY.md for
 private reporting

Add the security-advisory skill, adapted from the MCP Inspector's for a
single release line: the [GHSA-...] draft card, the ownership check (this
repo's server, an archived or third-party server, or the SDK underneath,
routed privately), the reach classes for filesystem, git and fetch, the
human-only accept / close / publish steps, the private fork, and
conversion to public tracking after publication. Eval cases included.

Add the two narrow advisory exceptions to AGENTS.md's board rules (a
[GHSA-...] draft card is the one allowed non-issue card; accepting an
advisory moves its unmilestoned draft from Incoming to Todo), the
draft-card lookup, create and convert recipes to board-ops, and a
pointer from issue-create's "never create a draft card".

Rewrite SECURITY.md: it told reporters the repo was not eligible, while
private vulnerability reporting is enabled and holds a backlog.

Refs #4870

Signed-off-by: cliffhall <cliff@futurescale.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
